### 2.1 Type Safety

-   Use TypeScript's strong typing system throughout the codebase
-   Avoid using `any` type whenever possible
-   Use type inference where appropriate but be explicit when it improves readability
-   Create dedicated type definitions for complex data structures

```typescript
// Prefer this:
interface User {
    id: string;
    name: string;
    email: string;
    role: UserRole;
    lastLogin?: Date;
}

// Over this:
const user: any = { id: '123', name: 'John' };
```

